          "path": "_m/s/w/8/w/aegina-wp/aegina-palaiochora-lat.jpg",
          "filename": "Aegina Palaiochora Ayios Georgios inscription.jpg",
          "caption": "Aegina, Palaiochora. Latin inscription over the northwest door of the church of Saint George (Ayios Georgios):\nTEMPORE SYNDICATUS CLARISS(IMI) DOMINI ANTONII BARBARO DIGNISIMI CONSILIARII NAUPLII ROMANIE DIE PRIMA APRILIS MDXXXIII\n\nThe inscription, dated 1 April 1533, commemorates the appointment of Zuan [i.e., Giovanni] Antonio Barbaro of Nauplia as the Venetian syndicus of Aegina. In the summer of 1533, shortly after completing his duties on Aegina and while on his way back to Nauplia, Barbaro was kidnapped and tortured by Turkish pirates. He was freed from the pirates by a Turkish officer but remained a prisoner on the island of Chios and died in captivity in July or August of that year, leaving a wife and five small children. See I diarii di Marino Sanuto, vol. 58 (Venice 1903), cols. 616–617. For the inscription, see W. Miller, The Latins in the Levant (London 1908), pp. 502–503, note 1.",
          "alt": "Aegina, Palaiochora. Latin inscription over the northwest door of the church of Saint George (Ayios Georgios):\nTEMPORE SYNDICATUS CLARISS(IMI) DOMINI ANTONII BARBARO DIGNISIMI CONSILIARII NAUPLII ROMANIE DIE PRIMA APRILIS MDXXXIII\n\nThe inscription, dated 1 April 1533, commemorates the appointment of Zuan [i.e., Giovanni] Antonio Barbaro of Nauplia as the Venetian syndicus of Aegina. In the summer of 1533, shortly after completing his duties on Aegina and while on his way back to Nauplia, Barbaro was kidnapped and tortured by Turkish pirates. He was freed from the pirates by a Turkish officer but remained a prisoner on the island of Chios and died in captivity in July or August of that year, leaving a wife and five small children. See I diarii di Marino Sanuto, vol. 58 (Venice 1903), cols. 616–617. For the inscription, see W. Miller, The Latins in the Levant (London 1908), pp. 502–503, note 1.",
          "width": 4387,
          "height": 2708,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "CC BY 4.0",
          "artist": "Mark Landon",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Aegina_Palaiochora_Ayios_Georgios_inscription.jpg",
          "sourceType": "core",
          "sourceArticleId": "aegina-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "sw8w",
          "mediumPath": "_m/s/w/8/w/aegina-wp/aegina-palaiochora-lat-medium.webp",
